From: SBE core-userland compatibility build
Subject: statefiles: preserve fd-relative PIO I/O on factory json-c 0.12

QSDK json-c 0.12 lacks later fd helpers and unsigned/array-capacity
constructors. Keep the secure openat() boundary, cap reads to 1 MiB and use
the older tokener/string APIs. Use the non-deprecated object lookup available
in 0.12, and provide the small mkdir-p helper missing from old libubox. PIO
prefix lengths are at most 128, so their signed int64 representation is exact.

